---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { rel, SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../../consts';
const description = 'Privacy policy for VibeRater by Dudley Development.';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy · VibeRater" description={description} path="/privacy/vibe-rater">
  <main class="page">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width:720px;">
      <a class="back" href={rel('/privacy/')}>← All privacy policies</a>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">VibeRater · Last updated July 8, 2026</p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        VibeRater is a free, for-entertainment app that gives your photos a playful AI "vibe" rating and,
        if you choose, lets you share ratings, post to a feed, add friends, message, and join events. When
        you rate a photo, it is <strong>sent to our service to generate the rating and then discarded —
        processed in memory and never stored</strong>. When you <strong>choose to post, share, or save</strong>,
        that media and the related profile and social data <strong>are stored</strong> so the feature works.
        We don't sell your personal data. Ads use Google AdMob, and you can say no to tracking with one tap.
      </p>

      <h2>Rating a photo (processed, not stored)</h2>
      <p>
        When you pick or take a photo to rate, VibeRater sends it to our rating service, which uses a
        third-party AI provider (Anthropic) to produce the playful score, verdict, archetype, and aura.
        <strong>A photo you only rate is used solely to generate that rating, processed in memory, and is
        never stored, retained, logged, or used to train models</strong>. The camera and photo-library
        permissions exist only so you can choose the image you want rated.
      </p>

      <h2>Accounts and profiles</h2>
      <p>
        Social features (posting, friends, messages, events, your Mini) use a profile that syncs to our
        cloud service so it stays attached to you across launches and devices. Depending on what you do,
        this can include: a device-generated account identifier; an optional username, display name, bio,
        avatar, and banner; and — if you choose to sign in — a Sign in with Apple or Google identifier
        (we receive an opaque identifier, not your Apple/Google password). You can use the rating features
        without creating a social profile.
      </p>

      <h2>Content you post or share</h2>
      <p>
        If you post, share, or save, the selected media and content — posts, captions, ratings you publish,
        vibe cards, comments, likes, events you create or RSVP to, and direct messages — <strong>are
        stored</strong> on our cloud infrastructure (Supabase) so the social features work and other users
        can see what you chose to share. Direct messages are stored to deliver them; they are not
        end-to-end encrypted, and we may access content when necessary for safety, moderation, or legal
        reasons. Content you rate privately (without posting) is never published.
      </p>

      <h2>Friends, contacts, and discovery</h2>
      <p>
        To help you find friends, VibeRater can scan the contacts on your device for saved @handles or
        invite codes. <strong>Your contacts are matched on-device and are not uploaded</strong>. If you opt
        in to VibeRadar (nearby discovery), a coarse, approximate location is shared briefly with other
        opted-in users so you can see nearby venues and vibers; you control this in Settings.
      </p>

      <h2>Safety and moderation</h2>
      <p>
        VibeRater has no tolerance for objectionable content or abusive users. You can report any post and
        block any user in the app. We review reports and act on them — typically within 24 hours — by
        removing content and, where warranted, removing the user. See our
        <a href={rel('/terms/vibe-rater')}>Terms of Use</a> for the full policy.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We use PostHog to understand how the app is used and to improve it. Analytics is limited to coarse,
        product events (for example, that a rating was completed) tied to your pseudonymous account
        identifier. <strong>We do not send your photos, messages, captions, names, or contacts to
        analytics.</strong> Event data is minimized and truncated, and if you enable private mode we stop
        sending analytics.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising (Google AdMob)</h2>
      <p>
        The app shows occasional ads served by <strong>Google AdMob</strong>, a third-party advertising
        network. To serve and measure ads, Google may collect device information such as the advertising
        identifier (IDFA), IP address, and coarse ad-interaction data. We do not receive, store, or link
        this to your account.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Your choice:</strong> the first time an ad is about to appear, iOS asks whether to allow tracking. If you choose <em>Ask App Not to Track</em>, you still get ads — just non-personalized ones.</li>
        <li><strong>Change your mind anytime:</strong> iOS Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → Tracking → VibeRater.</li>
        <li>How Google uses this data is described in <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" rel="noopener">Google's advertising policy</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google's privacy policy</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who we share data with</h2>
      <p>We do not sell your personal data. We share it only with the service providers that make the app work:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Anthropic</strong> — generates your vibe rating from a photo (processed in memory, not stored by us).</li>
        <li><strong>Supabase</strong> — cloud hosting and database for your profile and the content you post or share.</li>
        <li><strong>Apple &amp; Google</strong> — Sign in with Apple / Google sign-in, when you choose to use them.</li>
        <li><strong>Google AdMob</strong> — advertising, as described above.</li>
        <li><strong>PostHog</strong> — pseudonymous product analytics, as described above.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your recent results and any saved vibe cards.</li>
        <li>Your sign-in and session credentials, stored in the iOS Keychain.</li>
        <li>Your sound, haptics, language, and privacy preferences.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Retention and deleting your data</h2>
      <p>
        Content you post is retained until you delete it or delete your account. You can delete individual
        posts in the app, and you can <strong>delete your account</strong> from Settings, which removes your
        profile and associated social content and anonymizes your identifiers. Photos you only rate are
        never stored, so there is nothing to delete on our side.
      </p>

      <h2>For entertainment only</h2>
      <p>
        VibeRater is a novelty. Its scores, grades, archetypes, and auras are AI-generated fun and are not a
        measurement of anything real about you, your appearance, or any person in a photo.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        VibeRater is not directed at children under 13, and you must be at least 13 to use it. We do not
        knowingly collect personal information from children under 13.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        Data is transmitted over encrypted connections (HTTPS/TLS), sign-in and session credentials are held
        in the device Keychain, and access to stored content is controlled by your account. No method of
        transmission or storage is perfectly secure, but we take reasonable measures to protect your data.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes materially, the new version will be posted at this URL with an updated date
        above. Continued use of the app after a change constitutes acceptance.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions or data requests? Email <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
